WEBVTT

00:07.080 --> 00:08.420
Let's see.

00:09.160 --> 00:12.310
Shinjuku, Ikebukuro, Mejiro...

00:12.670 --> 00:14.100
Akasaka district.

00:14.900 --> 00:15.690
All right.

00:17.050 --> 00:19.820
Excuse me, but how long will it take to get to there?

00:19.980 --> 00:22.290
Uh, about 45 minutes.

00:22.290 --> 00:23.820
Okay, thank you.

00:48.460 --> 00:50.250
Give it your all.

00:50.620 --> 00:52.500
Make new friends.

00:53.020 --> 00:54.990
Go out and see the world.

00:55.130 --> 00:55.740
Okay.

00:57.830 --> 00:58.790
I'm leaving now.

01:04.410 --> 01:05.070
Sora!

01:06.580 --> 01:07.630
Sora!

01:10.550 --> 01:12.360
Hey, that's Tokyo Tower, isn't it?

01:12.720 --> 01:14.740
Amazing!

01:21.030 --> 01:23.180
This is... Tokyo.

03:17.000 --> 03:20.960
So then, this is your living allowance during your studies.

03:21.230 --> 03:24.950
Although it's not a lot, it should be enough if you use it wisely.

03:24.210 --> 03:25.190
I know.

03:26.760 --> 03:29.920
I apologize for not being able to give this to you last night.

03:30.500 --> 03:32.260
If that's all, I'll be going now.

03:32.840 --> 03:34.170
The training program...

03:35.170 --> 03:39.320
be careful and try not to give your teachers too much trouble.

03:39.690 --> 03:40.270
Sure.

03:41.690 --> 03:42.490
Gouta!

03:44.140 --> 03:49.170
I can take care of myself, old man. Worry about yourself first.

03:59.880 --> 04:00.610
Huh?

04:01.560 --> 04:03.720
Where's the station?

04:06.580 --> 04:08.020
I guess...

04:09.870 --> 04:12.950
I go straight, then immediately turn left...

04:15.500 --> 04:17.150
Why is there a lion?

04:18.970 --> 04:19.770
Ah!

04:23.190 --> 04:25.890
Ah, how many floors do you guys need?

04:27.320 --> 04:28.080
Huh, a river?

04:29.620 --> 04:31.620
Ah I see, it's a moat.

04:32.450 --> 04:35.980
"During the mid-summer, anybody can go fishing in the moat."

04:36.890 --> 04:41.250
Ah, don't give up, old man!

04:41.250 --> 04:42.700
I'll do my best too.

04:46.890 --> 04:52.010
Let's see, after crossing the #246 alley intersection of Sotobori Passway...

04:52.040 --> 04:53.730
I'll be in Akasaka?

04:53.760 --> 04:57.060
Then I should find the Metro...

05:16.060 --> 05:17.510
Granny, are you all right?

05:21.150 --> 05:23.580
Miss, what's the matter?

05:24.400 --> 05:25.610
I'm fine.

05:25.700 --> 05:28.140
I was just a bit surprised.

05:30.650 --> 05:32.020
Miss...

05:31.600 --> 05:33.140
Look after my bag, please!

05:33.140 --> 05:33.970
Bag?

05:41.170 --> 05:42.420
Stop!

05:51.020 --> 05:54.240
You're so brave! Thank you so much!

05:54.550 --> 05:56.140
Did you see that?

05:56.140 --> 05:57.860
You really saved us!

06:00.730 --> 06:02.400
Granny, can you stand?

06:08.920 --> 06:11.260
I'm fine, Nii-chan.

06:11.620 --> 06:13.510
Please be careful on the way home.

06:13.510 --> 06:15.650
All right, you be careful too.

06:18.500 --> 06:20.530
Um, are you all right?

06:22.360 --> 06:22.960
Yeah.

06:23.730 --> 06:26.220
That's great, everyone is safe.

06:26.640 --> 06:29.800
Was that your magic just now?

06:30.020 --> 06:30.740
Yes.

06:30.950 --> 06:32.830
But I'm not that great at it yet.

06:33.010 --> 06:35.640
It's okay from time to time if I move my hands somewhat...

06:35.810 --> 06:38.790
But when I have to concentrate on it...

06:38.090 --> 06:38.790
Thank you.

06:39.920 --> 06:43.920
Um, it's nothing. I'm currently heading to this place for magic training...

06:43.920 --> 06:44.710
Training?

06:44.830 --> 06:45.460
Yes.

06:45.460 --> 06:46.470
You don't need it.

06:47.430 --> 06:50.750
With that kind of mastery, why would you need training...

06:51.560 --> 06:52.230
Umm...

06:52.570 --> 06:57.160
I'm trying to find the Magic Bureau, but I don't know the Metro system very well.

06:57.620 --> 06:58.950
Then go walk around.

06:59.550 --> 07:01.470
More walking?

07:03.350 --> 07:06.050
The summers in Tokyo are really hot.

07:08.000 --> 07:09.940
I gained a lot of information from the police,

07:09.940 --> 07:12.050
and their iced mugi tea was really delicious..

07:14.800 --> 07:17.750
The ability to use magic is embedded in our DNA.

07:18.580 --> 07:21.570
In my case, my father was a mage.

07:23.220 --> 07:26.400
The level of magic ability differs between each individual.

07:26.620 --> 07:30.600
The power manifests itself in adolescence.

07:32.540 --> 07:36.000
At the age of 16, that person can finally begin training.

07:36.280 --> 07:39.880
And we have to be sent off to be trained.

07:41.230 --> 07:44.320
During training, there are two things that must occur;

07:45.020 --> 07:49.020
first is that we must reside with our teachers and train under them,

07:49.690 --> 07:53.960
and watch them perform the work of a mage to learn their abilities.

07:55.010 --> 07:59.890
And second, we have to learn magic history from the Magic Bureau as they oversee our training.

08:00.620 --> 08:03.460
Once you successfully complete the training,

08:03.460 --> 08:06.970
you will be registered as an official mage.

08:08.420 --> 08:10.660
The training period is one month.

08:17.640 --> 08:18.760
A family of cats...

08:19.520 --> 08:21.280
Give it your best, Mom.

08:27.790 --> 08:29.150
Just a bit further.

08:36.750 --> 08:40.530
Once you reach the Cultural Center...

08:42.590 --> 08:43.540
Is it this building?

08:44.690 --> 08:46.590
Ah, right next to it.

08:46.850 --> 08:47.910
How cute.

08:49.610 --> 08:51.160
So this is the Magic Bureau.

08:51.840 --> 08:54.390
This is where I'll become a mage.

08:55.320 --> 08:58.210
Father, I've arrived.

09:00.630 --> 09:03.220
Oh no! I'm so late! I've got to hurry!

09:03.690 --> 09:08.650
I'm sorry, um...  do you know the classroom for the magic training program?

09:08.880 --> 09:11.670
I'm sorry... um... the training...

09:16.250 --> 09:17.870
During this one month,

09:18.110 --> 09:23.320
you will study the fundamentals of magic and it's meaning in society

09:23.580 --> 09:28.790
We'll discuss all pratical applications of magic and any other thoughts you might have.

09:32.320 --> 09:34.090
Suzuki-san is the one who's late, right?

09:34.390 --> 09:36.000
Yes, I'm sorry.

09:36.160 --> 09:38.610
Well then, please introduce yourself.

09:39.010 --> 09:40.180
Huh? Okay...

09:40.180 --> 09:42.430
Everyone else has already done so.

09:42.730 --> 09:44.760
You are the last one.

09:44.940 --> 09:45.680
Yes.

09:46.950 --> 09:48.040
Pleased to meet you all.

09:48.240 --> 09:51.970
I came here from Biei, Hokkaido... I'm Suzuki Sora.

09:52.250 --> 09:56.950
And... I look forward to working hard with you all starting from today.

09:57.150 --> 09:59.470
Please treat me kindly.

09:59.860 --> 10:00.900
Is that all?

10:01.090 --> 10:01.820
Um...

10:02.530 --> 10:06.940
I have a pet dog named Chao, and my personal motto is "Trial and Error."

10:07.420 --> 10:08.140
That is all.

10:08.890 --> 10:11.420
Please be on time for class from now on.

10:11.420 --> 10:12.180
Yes.

10:12.640 --> 10:17.430
Being punctual is an integral part of being in society.

10:18.010 --> 10:19.550
Everyone should take heed of that.

10:19.550 --> 10:21.360
Yes, ma'am.

10:20.450 --> 10:22.470
Sora-chan, over here.

10:22.600 --> 10:25.770
Now that that is over with, everyone will be taking an aptitude test.

10:25.280 --> 10:27.020
Huh?

10:27.020 --> 10:30.560
In order to gauge your abilities,

10:30.560 --> 10:33.640
this test will be administered to see your understanding of magic.

10:33.910 --> 10:36.310
Damn it, a test already?

10:37.130 --> 10:39.700
Oohata-kun, please be quiet.

10:39.920 --> 10:42.220
Yes. What a pain...

10:42.610 --> 10:46.580
Now then, turn over the papers on your desk.

10:47.300 --> 10:48.370
You have twenty minutes.

10:49.040 --> 10:51.470
If you finish early, you are welcome to take a break.

10:51.730 --> 10:53.920
The skills test will begin at three o'clock.

10:54.300 --> 10:56.920
Before that, you must return to this classroom.

10:57.480 --> 10:58.460
Be on time.

11:00.190 --> 11:01.060
Yes.

11:07.650 --> 11:09.520
Sora-chan, would you like this?

11:09.520 --> 11:11.860
Sure, how much was it?

11:11.420 --> 11:13.480
It's fine, it's my treat.

11:13.480 --> 11:15.860
Wow, that's so nice of you! Thanks!

11:17.500 --> 11:21.160
That was so sudden. Your bag came flying at me!

11:23.400 --> 11:26.670
I'm Yamabuki Hiyori. Nice to meet you.

11:27.150 --> 11:31.250
My pleasure. I was kind of frightened...

11:31.250 --> 11:35.000
"I have a pet dog named Chao, and my personal motto is 'Trial and Error.'"

11:35.140 --> 11:35.880
"That is all."

11:35.880 --> 11:38.870
Hiyori-chan, stop making fun of me.

11:39.020 --> 11:41.410
Ah... okay.

11:46.560 --> 11:49.430
This is my first time being scolded for showing up late.

11:49.430 --> 11:52.080
Ah, that woman's name is Kawada.

11:52.320 --> 11:54.130
Kawada-sensei...

11:54.890 --> 11:56.730
What about the bodyguard looking guy next to her?

11:56.910 --> 11:57.980
Bodyguard?

11:58.680 --> 12:02.570
Ah, Morishita! That guy is Kawada-sensei's assistant.

12:02.570 --> 12:04.040
He looks like Kinpachi.

12:02.570 --> 12:05.510
Note: Kinpachi-sensei from third year, class B

12:03.790 --> 12:04.740
Yeah, totally!

12:06.830 --> 12:09.200
Huh, seems like everyone has returned to class.

12:09.620 --> 12:11.800
Well then, let's head back.

12:11.930 --> 12:13.830
This time we can't be late.

12:13.960 --> 12:14.630
Right?

12:22.580 --> 12:26.840
Today's skill test is manipulating water into ice.

12:27.620 --> 12:30.350
We're going to check your level of magic.

12:30.350 --> 12:31.310
Ice?

12:31.310 --> 12:32.770
That's so easy!

12:32.770 --> 12:34.070
Oohata-kun!

12:35.880 --> 12:40.660
Please pair up as a group with the person across from you.

12:40.790 --> 12:42.000
Group?

12:42.090 --> 12:44.790
Remember to help each other out.

12:44.890 --> 12:45.570
What?

12:46.720 --> 12:48.450
You're that guy from...

12:48.850 --> 12:52.170
Ah... Sora-chan, you know Midorikawa-kun?

12:52.760 --> 12:54.500
Not really, just a bit...

12:56.180 --> 12:58.540
I want to change groups.

12:58.890 --> 13:00.690
That guy gives me the creeps...

13:00.320 --> 13:02.080
Midorikawa-kun, correct?

13:02.240 --> 13:03.410
Care to explain your reason?

13:02.370 --> 13:03.760
Although he seems cool.

13:03.760 --> 13:04.510
Nothing.

13:04.760 --> 13:08.020
If you don't have a legitimate reason, then I will not allow you to change.

13:13.640 --> 13:14.640
Idiot!

13:15.630 --> 13:17.710
Wow, amazing!

13:17.780 --> 13:19.130
It's like ice paradise!

13:21.640 --> 13:23.480
So you can use magic too?

13:23.710 --> 13:24.860
Kind of...

13:25.850 --> 13:27.240
That's mine over there.

13:29.250 --> 13:30.990
It's like it was made.

13:31.390 --> 13:35.000
If you think about it, this is the most practical form for ice.

13:35.520 --> 13:38.290
This is useful magic, isn't it?

13:38.290 --> 13:39.650
I see.

13:40.970 --> 13:42.750
Suzuki-san is amazing.

13:42.750 --> 13:44.350
It's like a chandelier.

13:48.030 --> 13:49.130
I won't lose to you.

13:51.190 --> 13:53.810
Kawada-sensei, I have a question.

13:54.470 --> 13:55.870
What is it, Asagi-san?

13:57.010 --> 13:58.630
It's about Resurrection magic.

13:58.850 --> 14:01.690
I heard it is able to bring the dead back to life.

14:01.990 --> 14:02.950
Is that true?

14:03.720 --> 14:04.770
What a stupid question.

14:05.640 --> 14:09.780
It's a story made up by people who know nothing of magic.

14:10.270 --> 14:15.180
Regardless of the ability of the mage, life cannot be restored.

14:15.740 --> 14:16.700
Do you understand?

14:17.190 --> 14:18.470
Thank you.

14:18.870 --> 14:21.880
If you had thought about it, you would've realized that.

14:22.180 --> 14:23.460
And who are you?

14:23.470 --> 14:24.590
Kuroda Koji.

14:24.590 --> 14:27.840
I see, so you're knowledgeable in magic, aren't you?

14:27.840 --> 14:30.700
Not really, but that's why I'm here.

14:34.700 --> 14:35.410
What is it?

14:35.620 --> 14:37.190
Where is your water tank?

14:37.560 --> 14:38.710
Right next to yours.

14:40.310 --> 14:41.350
Are you copying me?

14:41.590 --> 14:42.400
What?

14:42.820 --> 14:44.120
That's it, isn't it?

14:44.300 --> 14:47.420
Anyone could've come up with a cylinder.

14:48.020 --> 14:51.080
Besides, mine has a hole so it can be carried.

14:51.430 --> 14:51.990
Huh?

14:52.570 --> 14:55.030
Both Asagi-san and Kuroda-san are amazing.

14:55.840 --> 14:59.790
For me, all I could do was turn it into ice.

15:00.100 --> 15:02.630
Well, that's what happens normally.

15:02.930 --> 15:06.820
But Suzuki-san's ice paradise is the most amazing.

15:08.310 --> 15:10.880
Where's the purpose in making icicles?

15:10.880 --> 15:13.630
Well, after all my years of being an assistant,

15:13.860 --> 15:17.160
this is the first time I've seen such wonderful and dynamic magic.

15:19.930 --> 15:22.020
I'll remake mine!

15:22.020 --> 15:23.230
Me too.

15:23.230 --> 15:25.650
Magic is not a competition.

15:26.100 --> 15:29.230
The essence of magic is something you have to look for yourself.

15:29.920 --> 15:31.590
I've finished photographing them all.

15:31.720 --> 15:32.640
What?

15:33.340 --> 15:35.460
After you have completed your training,

15:35.630 --> 15:38.380
you will need to know what kind of mage you'll be.

15:38.810 --> 15:40.900
That is the purpose of this training.

15:41.270 --> 15:44.350
Okay, class is over.

15:44.660 --> 15:48.310
Please return to your instructors now.

15:46.700 --> 15:48.710
Huh, Midorikawa-kun, what's the matter?

15:48.710 --> 15:51.170
Class will begin again tomorrow at 9am.

15:50.080 --> 15:51.990
You're a little slow aren't you, Kuroda Koji?

15:54.090 --> 15:56.010
Midorikawa-kun...

15:56.440 --> 15:58.470
Sora-chan, where is your instructor's place?

15:58.690 --> 16:01.650
Oh, I'm staying in the Shimokitazawa area.

16:01.400 --> 16:02.640
Wow, that's great!

16:02.640 --> 16:03.960
I'll have to come over sometime.

16:04.150 --> 16:05.770
Okay, what about you, Hiyori-chan?

16:05.770 --> 16:07.320
I'm at Azabujuuban.

16:08.010 --> 16:10.610
A lot of students aren't capable of manipulative magic.

16:10.610 --> 16:12.100
Don't be too hard on yourself.

16:14.460 --> 16:16.630
Would you like to help me clean up?

16:17.210 --> 16:17.920
Sure.

16:19.630 --> 16:21.250
See you tomorrow, then.

16:21.250 --> 16:23.640
Okay, thanks for everything today.

16:26.990 --> 16:28.980
Suzuki-san, are you all right?

16:29.310 --> 16:32.190
I'm wondering if I can get used to this...

16:32.480 --> 16:33.970
What's the matter? Did something happen?

16:33.970 --> 16:36.170
It's nothing, I'm just tired.

16:37.680 --> 16:39.100
Why are you laughing?

16:39.250 --> 16:42.410
Oh, sorry. It's obvious that you're tired.

16:42.670 --> 16:45.690
You just arrived from Hokkaido today, right?

16:45.900 --> 16:46.540
Yes.

16:46.690 --> 16:48.190
Then that is why you're so tired.

16:48.190 --> 16:49.400
It would be weird if you weren't.

16:49.400 --> 16:50.370
I see.

16:50.750 --> 16:53.030
Tomorrow, the real training will begin.

16:53.790 --> 16:54.970
Aren't you excited?

16:55.190 --> 16:59.320
That's right, I'll have to give it my all from now on.

16:59.620 --> 17:01.290
Kuroda-kun, thank you.

17:03.170 --> 17:05.160
Suzuki-san, are you heading to Shimokitazawa?

17:05.160 --> 17:05.790
Yes.

17:05.790 --> 17:07.510
Then you should take the Metro from Kasumi...

17:08.280 --> 17:13.440
From the Shimokitazawa station north exit, make a right turn...

17:16.790 --> 17:22.860
Now then, I'm going to sing this song that just suddenly came to mind.

17:23.490 --> 17:24.620
It's a song about jellyfish.

18:55.920 --> 18:57.860
Michiru, Tokyo...

18:57.860 --> 19:01.250
Shimokitazawa is such an amazing place!

19:01.790 --> 19:05.420
I visited so many shops it was like finding treasure!

19:05.690 --> 19:07.900
It's like a country from my dreams.

19:09.970 --> 19:12.760
There are a lot of old and new things all intermixed.

19:13.510 --> 19:16.920
Michiru... I think I'm starting to love this city.

19:19.050 --> 19:21.040
I'm going to give it my best!

19:26.240 --> 19:29.300
Wow, this bench is so huge!

19:32.170 --> 19:35.360
Um, it's Suzuki from Biei.

19:36.390 --> 19:40.280
Um, I'm the one from Biei, Hokkaido... Suzuki...

19:40.690 --> 19:42.390
It's Sora-chan, right?

19:42.760 --> 19:43.500
Yes.

19:43.700 --> 19:44.700
Come on in.

19:45.010 --> 19:46.950
I was a bit worried since you were late.

19:47.700 --> 19:51.410
I'm sorry, there were so many interesting things to look at.

19:51.410 --> 19:52.580
They were all so cute.

19:52.580 --> 19:55.870
Oh really? Is this your first time in Shimokitazawa?

19:56.020 --> 19:58.700
Yes, it's all so surreal...

19:59.670 --> 20:03.320
There was a woman near the station who was singing a song that was really good!

20:06.230 --> 20:08.260
Welcome to Shimokitazawa.

20:08.480 --> 20:10.920
Yes, pleasure to be here.

20:13.150 --> 20:14.230
Hara-sensei.

20:14.770 --> 20:19.430
I'm really thankful you'll be instructing me from now on.

20:20.030 --> 20:21.730
Yeah. Good luck.

20:22.060 --> 20:22.730
Yes!

20:23.070 --> 20:25.330
Sora-chan's room is the first one on the second floor.

20:25.620 --> 20:26.930
Take a break until dinner.

20:27.210 --> 20:29.650
Today has been very tiring.

20:30.660 --> 20:34.120
Oh, Sawari-chan is looking after the other trainee, but we can work that out later.

20:34.120 --> 20:36.330
There's another trainee here?

20:36.330 --> 20:38.520
Yeah, I'll introduce you two later.

20:38.640 --> 20:39.390
Okay.

20:53.150 --> 20:54.270
This is...

20:56.120 --> 20:58.270
A guy's room?

20:59.040 --> 21:00.340
How come?

21:11.990 --> 21:14.950
Father, I've made it to Tokyo.

21:23.880 --> 21:26.370
Ah, there's a garden!

21:30.320 --> 21:31.390
No way...

21:31.960 --> 21:34.260
It's that other trainee...

21:35.220 --> 21:36.200
Why is that?

23:05.510 --> 23:08.550
Motohashi-san lives in such a big building.

23:08.920 --> 23:13.370
And she's going to be my very first magic client.

23:13.870 --> 23:15.210
Next time, Sora.

23:15.870 --> 23:18.610
I wonder if my magic will be enough.
